---
title: Stir-fried Bean Sprouts (Chao Dou Ya 炒豆芽)
description: A crunchy, fresh, and incredibly fast side dish. Mung bean sprouts are briefly stir-fried with scallions and a touch of vinegar.
prep time: 5 minutes
cook time: 2 minutes
servings: 2
tags:
  - bean sprouts
  - vegetable
  - quick
  - chinese
  - side
cuisine: Chinese
course: Side
---

> The key to perfect bean sprouts is extremely high heat and adding vinegar early to help them retain their crunch.

== Prepare Ingredients ==

Rinse the @mung bean sprouts{200%g} and drain them very thoroughly. Any excess water will make them steam instead of fry.
Chop the @scallion{1%stalk} into 2-inch segments.
Mince the @garlic{2%cloves}.

== Stir-fry ==

Heat a #wok{} over the highest heat possible until it's smoking slightly. Add @neutral oil{1%tbsp}.

Quickly add the minced garlic and scallion segments. Toss for ~{5%seconds}.

Immediately add the bean sprouts. Toss rapidly for ~{15%seconds}.

== Season and Finish ==

Drizzle @rice vinegar{1%tsp} down the side of the wok so it sizzles. This helps keep the sprouts crunchy. Toss to mix.

Add:
- @salt{¼%tsp}
- @chicken bouillon powder{¼%tsp} (optional)

Toss for another ~{15%seconds} until just wilted but still very crunchy.

Drizzle with a few drops of @toasted sesame oil{½%tsp}. Give it a final toss and serve immediately.